  "notes": [
    "Transcribed by hand from the pages above on the retrieval date. Always confirm against the live AMD documentation before relying on a result.",
    "Every rule carries a 'ref' list naming entries in 'references': the exact page, section and row, the ROCm version that page describes, the transcription date and the date the rule was last re-checked against that page. A reference that could not be re-checked has verification 'unverified' and says why.",
    "The system-requirements page (7.14-era) and the 10.1.0 compatibility matrix disagree on some OS point releases (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04.4 vs 24.04.5). Both are recorded and either source counts as a match.",
    "os_gpu_restrictions name individual products, because GPUs that share an LLVM target can differ (e.g. MI300X and MI300A on Debian 13). Where the 10.1.0 matrix and the 7.14 system requirements disagree about a GPU on an OS, the GPU counts as supported if either page lists it, the same rule as for the OS lists.",
    "Some GPU-to-target mappings in the 10.1.0 matrix (Radeon series rows, Ryzen APUs) were ambiguous in the published table; those targets are listed under targets_uncertain and produce WARNING, never PASS.",
    "Per AMD: if a GPU is not listed it is not officially supported."
  ],
